  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many tortilla chips Nancy kept for herself, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Start with the total number of tortilla chips Nancy has.\n2. Subtract the number of tortilla chips she gave to her brother.\n3. Subtract the number of tortilla chips she gave to her sister.\n\nLet's go through the calculations step by step:\n\n1. Nancy starts with 22 tortilla chips.\n2. She gives 7 tortilla chips to her brother. So, we subtract 7 from 22:\n   \\[\n   22 - 7 = 15\n   \\]\n3. She then gives 5 tortilla chips to her sister. So, we subtract 5 from the remaining 15:\n   \\[\n   15 - 5 = 10\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of tortilla chips Nancy kept for herself is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).",
